/**
 * @defgroup raze_options Options
 * @brief Compile-time modifiers attached to algorithms via `operator[]`.
 *
 * Options can be chained in any order (e.g., `algo[opt1][opt2](...)`). Repeating a keyed option
 * replaces the previous value. Individual algorithm pages only document non-default configurations
 * and algorithm-specific option behavior (such as `aligned<...>` arity); standard modifier semantics
 * are defined here and in @ref dynamic_dispatch / @ref vectorization_semantics.
 *
 * ### Quick Reference
 *
 * | Option | Effect |
 * | :--- | :--- |
 * | `raze::options::fscalar` | Disables SIMD and compiler auto-vectorization; guarantees strict sequential in-order execution. |
 * | `raze::options::fstatic` | Disables runtime CPUID dispatch and compiles strictly for the static target ISA. |
 * | `raze::options::fautovec` | Bypasses `raze::vx::simd` probing and selects compiler auto-vectorization when available (falls back to scalar otherwise). |
 * | `raze::options::unroll<N>` | Sets the manual SIMD loop unrolling factor (`unroll<1>` disables unrolling; has no effect on `autovec` or scalar paths). |
 * | `raze::options::aligned<Ns...>` | Declares minimum byte alignment(s) for contiguous range pointers (broadcast `aligned<N>` or positional `aligned<N1, ...>`). Supported only on algorithms that document it. |
 * | `raze::options::unaligned` | Readable alias for `1` inside positional `aligned<...>` lists. |
 * | `raze::options::strict_types` | Disables implicit `std::common_type_t` promotion in mixed-type binary SIMD algorithms (e.g., binary `transform`). |
 * | `raze::options::par` | Enables multi-threaded parallel execution (orthogonal to `fscalar`, `fautovec`, `fstatic`). |
 * | `raze::options::grain_size<N>` | Minimum parallel chunk size in elements (effective with `par`). |
 * | `raze::options::threads<N>` | Maximum worker thread count (effective with `par`). |
 *
 * @see @ref dynamic_dispatch
 * @see @ref vectorization_semantics
 */

/**
 * @page raze_vx_options SIMD Options (`raze::vx`)
 *
 * Functors in `raze::vx` accept compile-time option flags via `operator[]` (often combinable
 * with @ref mask_semantics):
 *
 * | Option | Applies to | Semantics |
 * |--------|------------|-----------|
 * | `raze::vx::aligned` | `load`, `store`, `compress_store` | Uses aligned load/store instructions (`alignof(V)` required). |
 * | `raze::vx::safe` | `load`, `store` | Guarantees masked-out memory lanes are never read or written. |
 * | `raze::vx::unsafe` | `compress_store` | Allows overwriting trailing lanes up to `V::size()` for speed. |
 * | `raze::vx::not_null` | `find_first_set`, `find_first_not_set`, `find_last_set`, `find_last_not_set`, `find_next_set`, `clear_first`, `clear_last` | Assumes at least one matching lane exists, skipping empty-mask checks (UB if violated). |
 * | `raze::vx::uniform` | `fold` | Returns a SIMD vector with the reduced value broadcast to all lanes. |
 * | `raze::vx::saturated` | `convert` | Performs clamping (saturating) conversion instead of truncation. |
 * | `raze::vx::ignore_unsupported` | `convert` | Returns input unchanged when `T` is not an arithmetic type. |
 */

